-- title:
--   Finite index of speciality for function fields over K(X)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and let $F$ be a field carrying both a $K$-algebra structure and a $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,K$-algebra structure, compatibly (a scalar tower $K \subseteq \mathrm{RatFunc}\,K \subseteq F$), such that $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the rational function field $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,K = K(X)$. Assume further: `HasPrincipalDivisors K F`, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ admits a finitely supported function $D$ on the places of $F/K$ (a place being a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring) with $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v(f)$ for all $v$ and $\deg D = \sum_v D(v)\,\deg v = 0$; `IsCurveOver K F`, which in addition to principal divisors requires that each residue field $v$ be a finite-dimensional $K$-module and that $\Omega_{F/K}$ be a free $F$-module of rank $1$; that at least one place of $F/K$ exists; and that the Riemann–Roch space of the zero divisor, $\{f \in F : v(f) \le 1 \text{ for all } v\}$, be a finite-dimensional $K$-vector space. The conclusion is `IndexOfSpecialtyFinite K F`: there is a divisor $D_0$, i.e. a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on the places, such that the quotient of the adele space `adeleSpace K F` (the supremum inside $\prod_v F$ of the submodules `adeleBdd D` over all divisors $D$) by the submodule generated by the part of `adeleBdd D₀` and the part of `globalSub K F` lying in the adele space is a finite $K$-module.
--
--   This is the finiteness of the index of speciality $i(D_0) = \dim_K \mathbb{A}_F/(\mathbb{A}_F(D_0) + F) < \infty$ for a finite separable extension of a rational function field, the adelic finiteness underlying the Riemann–Roch theorem for such function fields. It is used to produce places with prescribed order behaviour, in [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_place_notMem_ord_neg_and_forall_ord_eq_one`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_place_notMem_ord_neg_and_forall_ord_eq_one).
